      <tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:yotzer_or/hameir" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n102.jpg">
        <j:conditional xml:id="yotzer_hameir_condition">
          <j:all>
            <tei:fs type="opensiddur:holiday-aggregate">
              <tei:f name="shabbat">
                <tei:binary value="false"/>
              </tei:f>
            </tei:fs>
          </j:all>
        </j:conditional>
        <tei:p><tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n102.jpg" n="37"/>He who lights the earth and those who dwell on it, with mercy and daily in His goodness constantly renews the work of creation.  <tei:milestone unit="chapter" n="104"/><tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/104/24" n="24"/><tei:seg source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:psalms/104/24">How numerous are Thy works, O Lord, all of them hast Thou made with wisdom, the earth is full of Thy possessions. </tei:seg> <tei:milestone unit="verse"/><tei:milestone unit="chapter"/>O King, who alone is exalted from of old, extolled and praised and glorified since days of antiquity. O God of eternity, in Thy great mercy have mercy upon us, <tei:pb ed="1965" facs="https://archive.org/download/mahzor-lyom-rishon-shel-rosh-hashanah-day-one-jenny-marmorstein-1965/page/n104.jpg" n="38"/>Lord of our might, Rock of our fortress, shield of our salvation, a fortress around us. </tei:p>
        <j:endConditional target="#yotzer_hameir_condition"/>
      </tei:div>
    </tei:body>
  </tei:text>
